## Report
Validated the suspected logic bug in commit fe8663b4. I added a targeted unit PoC inside crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs and ran it against the real storage crate. The PoC constructs a committed floor PgMetadataProof { applied_log_index: 42, applied_log_hash: 0xaaa, state_digest: 0x111 } and an observed proof { applied_log_index: 43, applied_log_hash: 0xdead_beef, state_digest: 0x222 }. Despite the different hash and digest, validate_peering_metadata_proof_floor(...).is_ok() succeeds, and peering_metadata_read_route_for_snapshot returns a PgMetadataReadRoute containing the divergent observed proof. Command output: `running 1 test ... security_poc_peering_read_route_accepts_higher_divergent_metadata_proof ... ok`. Debugger evidence: lldb breakpoint at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:22727 showed active_floor=(index=42, hash=2730, digest=273), observed=(index=43, hash=3735928559, digest=546), with stack frame #1 in validate_peering_metadata_proof_floor at control_plane.rs:23044. Code evidence: control_plane.rs:22723-22728 accepts `observed.applied_log_index > active_floor.applied_log_index || observed == active_floor`; control_plane.rs:23020-23044 uses that predicate for peering floor validation; control_plane.rs:4738-4768 selects a peering metadata read route and stores `observation.metadata_proof` as the route proof. Downstream, local.rs:4135-4149 converts a Peering route into MetadataReadAuthorization::peering, request_ops.rs:9729-9744 uses metadata_pg_read_node/open_object_read_metadata_route for object read authorization, and node.rs:1453-1457 only checks the current observation equals the route proof and has no pending command, not that the proof equals or descends from the committed floor. I attempted a crash-style reproduction via the test harness; no crash is expected because this is an authorization/certification logic flaw. Valgrind was attempted but unavailable in the container (`valgrind not installed in container; memory checking not applicable to this logic flaw`).

